WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
That's the speech of the Satan. He always gives us a chance again to fight against the Satan.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:12.000
But although that's not the speech of the Satan, yes, the Satan still can speak and that is the weapon of the Satan.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
That's why I was going to tell you later on that he's going to bite you with his mouth.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
You know? He's going to bite you, the Satan.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Now when he's going to mouth the speech of the Satan, he's going to still have the power to paralyze you.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Why is it a Nahash? Why is it a Nahash? A person can just bite you, a very small bite, but it's a viral injection. It poisons you.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:40.000
It's beautiful, you know. A small little hole, like a needle, you know. A little bite.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:49.000
You know, and with this mouth, the Satan, just a little bite, small like a needle, paralyzes your body, turns it on and kills the person.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:56.000
We're going to see that yes, at the time of Den Haas, we're going to see that there is

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:03.200
Mr. Labrador, we're going to see, we're going to see, we're going to see, Satan eats, and

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.860
he eats from our heart, we're going to see, we're going to see, see for me this part of

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:11.740
the Torah is more important than the first chapter, the first chapter is about the creation

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:16.440
of the world, it's important, but for me this is more important because this is about the

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:23.160
nature and behavior of man. How man behaves. You know? And since we are humans, this is

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:26.360
closer to us than Shaman Ba'al is. Because he's talking about us.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:35.060
No, because he's obviously talking only about the Israelite.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:40.200
You sort of mentioned a perfect environment. How do you explain that it's a perfect environment

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.460
where there's a thing like a snake around?

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:46.240
That's the point. Although the environment is perfect, and so on, man has the possibility.

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:53.240
This is what is telling you in the Torah. Even in the best state, yes, in the best environment, you have the possibility of perversion.

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:59.240
And this is part of man's nature. We are going to see how to combat this. The Torah tells us how to combat this.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:05.240
But there is a way to fight it. But no matter how good the environment is, that's why, you know, it's relevant to us,

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:15.240
change the environment all over, you have the best environment, man can and will become perverted unless there is Esa Chayim.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:16.140
what does it mean to have a heart?

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:17.800
But then it wasn't a perfect environment

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:18.680
as you would describe.

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:20.100
No, it's not a question that is there.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:21.620
Animals are more friendly

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:24.120
and the environment is more friendly.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:24.640
I tell you,

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:26.340
because this Nahash

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:27.900
is in the nature of man.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:28.600
So now,

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:30.220
no matter how good your

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:32.320
the outside world is,

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.800
still we have the Nahash inside

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:37.280
and there is only one place.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:39.120
The answer means to combat the Nahash

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:40.740
is by eating from Esa Hayim.

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:42.780
And what is the Esa Hayim?

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:43.640
We're going to see later on.

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:45.140
Esa Hayim was given to us

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:48.040
that's the Trump, there was the Eta Chaim in the Mahajikim Bar,

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:51.040
and then Mechia and Ushar, we have this with the Eta Chaim,

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:56.440
and if we don't eat from this Eta Chaim, we have no antidote against the Nahash biting.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:03:00.240
We need to see this, but this is going to become very clear from now on.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:02.440
Mr. Shomer, one more question, because I have to go and cover it.

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:05.240
This is the one thing, this snake actually didn't talk?

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:07.240
This talk, of course it talked.

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:09.240
It is a lie.

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:10.240
With an Adan?

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:12.240
With an Adan, with Havah.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.240
You know, it begins with Chabad and I'll tell you what it is.

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:17.240
This is the way the Zohar explains it.

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:21.240
It's not a snake in the sense that it's a...

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:25.240
You know, it's a symbolism for Satan.

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:28.240
And it's not a snake because how do we know that it's not a regular snake?

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:31.240
Even Azra says, the regular snake...

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:33.240
Does it speak the regular snake?

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:36.240
So here God tells to the snake, tells it, don't crawl on your belly.

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:39.240
But it doesn't tell to the snake stop speaking.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:57.240
Whatever it is, you could say this. But even Asya, the Zohar also says, the Haram-Ban, the Ram-Ban, all the Hakamim, the Rees-Hakam-Alamin, all of them, they say, Nahashiah does not mean a regular snake. It means symbolism for...

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:58.080
Or, uh...

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:00.040
Why did he punish the actual snake?

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:01.980
No, he did not punish the actual snake.

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:02.540
We're going to see.

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:05.300
Do you think that the actual snake only eats dust?

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:06.760
Well, cool.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:08.220
Cool, but doesn't eat dust?

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:10.320
Doesn't eat dust?

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:10.620
No.

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:16.700
But doesn't eat dust?

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:18.820
So, obviously,

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:19.960
he's not talking about the regular snake.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:22.640
The snake actually did not exist.

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:23.960
It was a figment of his imagination?

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:25.540
No, he said,

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:27.540
It's not a figment of our reality, it's a real thing.

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:29.020
But you have to know how to fight.

