00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:16.960
which is right in the middle of the garden

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:21.200
do not eat from it

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:22.780
and don't touch it

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:26.320
because otherwise you might die.

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:27.460
In other words,

00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:28.880
Nahash, he says,

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:32.260
God forbid you to not to eat

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:34.500
from all the trees of the

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:35.440
valley? He says, no.

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:38.280
Only from one. So the Nahash says to the women,

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:40.040
think about it. Why only from one?

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:41.880
Why only from one?

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:44.080
God forbid you not to eat

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:46.300
from all the other trees? Only from one.

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:48.520
Why only from this particular one?

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:55.160
Of course you're not going to die.

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:00.760
The day you're going to eat it,

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:02.620
you're going to die.

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:05.100
The day you're going to eat it,

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:06.460
you're going to die.

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:08.040
We're going to see what's the meaning of it,

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.540
because it doesn't die that very day.

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:10.780
We're going to see what's the meaning of it.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:12.300
But he told them,

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:14.100
in the day that you're going to eat from it,

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:14.740
you're going to die.

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:16.380
Now the rabbis, they say about

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:17.600
the secret of the woman,

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:21.480
And here you see, sometimes women want to become too religious.

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:23.000
So what happened with the women?

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:27.420
God told the women, or to Adam, do not eat from the tree.

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:32.700
So God said to the women, not only we may not eat it, we may not even touch it.

00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:35.620
God didn't say don't touch it.

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:36.400
He said don't eat it.

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:43.980
So from here, God means, whoever becomes too extreme at one point, he's goreah.

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:46.180
He misses on the other point.

00:06:46.180 --> 00:06:47.580
The women at the beginning became too extreme,

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:50.420
said that even we're not allowed to touch it.

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:52.860
So the story, the Midyat says that the Nahash

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:55.060
pushed the women to the tree.

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:57.060
And she touched it, nothing happened.

00:06:57.060 --> 00:06:58.900
Nothing happened to her.

00:06:58.900 --> 00:07:00.240
She went and she ate it.

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:02.700
Now sometimes when we become over religious,

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:03.900
so what happened?

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:08.120
One day we transgress the superfluous part,

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:10.380
and say well, we transgress the superfluous part,

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:13.620
nothing happened to us, let's go and eat from the tree itself.

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:17.740
Sometimes it doesn't pay to become, you know, over-religious.

00:07:17.860 --> 00:07:18.940
Middle of the road.

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:20.380
Middle of the road.

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:21.980
No, right there in the middle of the road.

00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:23.140
Oh, right there in the middle of the road.

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:31.880
Now, by Yomer, Nahash, and Aisha.

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:36.500
Yeah, well, this is pertaining to the material, but in your statement.

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:38.340
Of course, this is only a midrash, and I said that.

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:39.580
Yeah, what do you mean by two religions?

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:41.460
By two religions, I mean specifically.

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:50.520
The Torah, there are 613 commandments, you know, and what the law is, is being clearly formulated by Shoham Al-Aruch.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:56.820
And the other thing is up to you to do it or not to do it.

00:07:57.020 --> 00:08:02.780
When you want to become over-religious sometimes, people want to become so religious at the end,

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:05.020
because from one extreme to another extreme.

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:10.960
You are, I mean, from my point of view, what is obligatory is what is written in Shoham Al-Aruch.

00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:15.460
And the Quran is very clearly what is haram and what is halal.

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:21.960
People who add things to earth, sometimes they are not aware that they add so much,

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:30.660
so much that people cannot just withstand that kind of pressure and then at the end they leave everything.

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:36.960
This is a very, very dangerous world and I certainly, I oppose that kind of...

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:39.860
You know, we have to do what the Torah tells you, not more, not less.

00:08:39.860 --> 00:08:42.600
And Chava, you see, she was very religious.

00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:45.720
She said, not even to touch it.

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:48.280
And then she was, you know, she fell into a trap.

00:08:48.580 --> 00:08:50.460
What do you mean by Oseke de Latora?

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:52.080
Who Oseke de Latora?

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:52.880
Hakamim.

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:55.360
Ah, Salam Tamar. Very good.

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:55.960
Hakamim.

00:08:56.480 --> 00:09:00.040
Now, as we know, you know, as we know,

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:03.380
Hakamim, we had Hakamim.

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:05.560
At the time we had Sanadim, we had Tatin and so on.

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:08.140
But the last group of Hakamim that we had,

00:09:08.140 --> 00:09:15.140
There was the ha-harim of all the Shia who had the right to do whatever they wanted to do to make this extra face where the rabbis of the Talmud.

00:09:15.140 --> 00:09:17.140
That's why the Talmud is obligatory for us.

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:26.140
Now the Shom Ha-Haruch and the Rambam are based exclusively according to the minhach of our own Sephardic communities.

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:32.140
So these people had the wisdom and the intelligence to know and the authority

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:35.200
to make sometimes

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:37.080
very occasionally, very rarely

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:39.060
extra law

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:40.560
extra things

00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:42.340
but the rest of the people

00:09:42.340 --> 00:09:45.100
unfortunately

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:46.120
Masha'i hasn't come yet

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:49.020
we know we are doing what the Torah says

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:50.020
what the Rabbam says

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:52.780
we have our maqamim, that's what we do

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:55.160
but you want to do it, you may do it

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:57.200
but you have no right

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:58.920
to tell to other people you must do it

00:09:58.920 --> 00:10:00.380
you know

00:10:00.380 --> 00:10:05.460
which one chooses his own mode, but he has no right to tell other people,

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:07.600
for instance, somebody to say about blood culture.

00:10:09.720 --> 00:10:13.080
He's ill. I have no, I don't oppose anyone,

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:15.080
and I'm saying anyone who wants to eat blood culture,

00:10:15.520 --> 00:10:18.500
the whole of Mosque just needs to know.

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:21.200
But obligatory to say that it's obligatory,

00:10:21.580 --> 00:10:24.440
that if I don't eat, I'm eating the left, this has no right to tell me.

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:25.960
This is the difference.

00:10:25.960 --> 00:10:29.280
The one to eat it, for instance, women sometimes,

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:32.780
the ones, you know, like the cover, they cut their hair, what?

00:10:33.580 --> 00:10:34.500
What are you going to do?

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:38.060
Would you say that is the difference between Hasidic and Orthodox?

00:10:38.760 --> 00:10:41.960
I don't know, I don't know, I don't like to use only words like this, because it's not

00:10:41.960 --> 00:10:42.360
a label.

00:10:42.580 --> 00:10:46.740
I like to say, very simple, we have Shukran Al-Rukh, Shukran Al-Rukh is what's haram,

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:50.700
it's what's halal, you know, that's what the Shukran Al-Rukh says, and this is why

00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:55.280
I'm obligated to observe the Jum, Shukran Al-Rukh, that is an obligation.

00:10:55.280 --> 00:11:01.280
Other thing, you know, it's not enough with what the Torah has made.

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:04.280
So we add to what the Torah has made.

00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:09.280
Same thing, they want to use it, very good. They want to go beyond, very good.

00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:12.280
I have nothing against certain thoughts.

00:11:12.280 --> 00:11:21.280
However, to say that I, or you, or him, must cropil, that's why the question has used me.

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:25.280
I am, you know, I want to make extra in the prayer house.

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:27.280
There were always, we had Hasidim.

00:11:27.280 --> 00:11:28.280
But what does Hasidim mean?

00:11:28.280 --> 00:11:32.280
They were a few people who upon themselves,

00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:35.280
they could have understood the Torah maybe a bit better than we did.

00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:38.280
Or because they spoiled more responsibility.

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:41.280
And themselves in a very humble way, they did it.

00:11:41.280 --> 00:11:45.280
As the Gemara says, you know, there's 36 Hasidim in the world every time.

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:48.280
But nobody knows you. Nobody knows you.

00:11:48.280 --> 00:11:51.960
You know the story? I want to tell you the story.

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:53.180
I'm sorry to interrupt.

00:11:54.660 --> 00:11:55.840
Let me tell you the story.

00:11:56.300 --> 00:11:57.840
The story is a very deep story.

00:11:59.300 --> 00:12:00.060
In Safed,

00:12:00.260 --> 00:12:01.320
in Safed, at one time

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:04.080
Safed was the city

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:04.740
of Kabbalah.

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:05.920
The people in Kabbalah were in Safed.

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:08.280
All of them were in Safed.

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:10.600
And there was a

00:12:10.600 --> 00:12:12.600
haqqan who knew how

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:13.880
to pray at the Kabbalah.

00:12:16.480 --> 00:12:17.500
So he wants

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:24.500
